  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 138 AM EDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nIsolated patchy frost for parts of far northeast TN and southwest VA \nthis morning. Increasing morning lows will diminish the potential \nfor frost development for most. However, dense fog near waterways \ncould be possible with colder air over top warmer waters in lakes \nand rivers.\n\nFor the week ahead, longwave troughing will remain well into Canada \nwith ridging poking north between a closed upper low off of the Mid-\nAtlantic and another closed low off of the west coast. A pseudo-\nOmega block pattern. The western low eventually phases with the mean \nflow, meanwhile the Atlantic one expected to bring coastal issues to \nparts of the Eastern Seaboard due to hardly any movement, will \nbecome enveloped and shunted east towards the end of the week. No \nimpacts here except persistent upper level ridging and surface high \npressure.\n\nHighs will remain in the low to mid (some upper) 70s range the rest \nof the forecast period into early next week. A general \nwash/rinse/repeat each day with light winds, mostly sunny/clear \nskies, low humidity, and no precipitation for at least the \nforeseeable future.",
